{"availability":"available","full":"miksrv/arduino-weather-station","name":"arduino-weather-station","description":"Arduino Weather Station is an automated weather monitoring project built on Arduino for collecting environmental data, featuring an API (PHP + MySQL + CodeIgniter) and a web interface (Next.js + Redux RTK) for real-time and historical weather data analysis. Please give the project a star :)","category":"Developer tools","language":"PHP","stars":97,"forks":7,"created":"2020-02-27T05:20:28Z","updated":"2026-10-05T01:07:28Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://meteo.miksoft.pro","topics":["arduino","nextjs","react","typescipt","weather","weather-app"],"demo":"https://meteo.miksoft.pro/en","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T08:59:07.588Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T08:59:07.588Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T08:59:07.588Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T08:59:07.588Z","stars":97,"forks":7}],"technologies":["React","Next.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Arduino Weather Station is a complete DIY weather-monitoring project powered by Arduino or ESP32. It collects real environmental data and provides a full backend API (PHP + MySQL + CodeIgniter) and a modern web interface (Next.js + Redux RTK) for real-time and historical weather analysis. You can use this repository to build your own fully-featured weather station - and if you like it, please give the project a star :)","Arduino Weather Station is a modular DIY platform for collecting and analyzing weather data. It supports Arduino or ESP32, works with a wide range of sensors, and sends real-time measurements to a backend server. Data is processed, stored, and exposed through a clean REST API and a modern Next.js dashboard."],"features":["Live data: continuous sensor monitoring.","Historical logging: long-term storage in MySQL with detailed analytics.","Web dashboard: access your station from anywhere — charts, stats, trends.","REST API: i